  "_comment": "Real Pixabay photos for the junk image files scattered through the machine (Downloads, Pictures, phone backup, and the like) that carry no story significance - camera-roll clutter, not evidence. Replaces the procedural gray-ish gradient render for these specific files. A file's folder decides its category (longest matching prefix wins, 'life' is the default for anything unmatched); within a category a file picks one photo deterministically from a hash of its own path, the same way lib/synth.ts picks a filler scene. `overrides` pins a handful of files whose own name already says what they are (a saved 'cat.jpg' should be a cat) to an exact photo instead of a hash. Fetched by `npm run fetch:assets` and on first run (see web/lib/fetchAssets.ts) into generated/filler-photo/<category>-<id>.jpg; until fetched (no PIXABAY_API_KEY set) these files fall back to the old procedural render.",
